    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1117">

                <pb facs="1138" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.4016/287a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-16T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2758. Reports have reached the Department that situation of Armenian exiles in
                    Mesopotamia is daily becoming worse—that great numbers are dying of hunger and
                    sickness, and children are sold openly in markets. If true, again urge Turkish
                    Government in name of humanity to alleviate condition remnants of this race.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
